Subject: [PATCH 07310/11362] [outer-loop] update
 GAP-ARCH-FRAME-CHANGE-PREDICTOR: candidate design falsified

Per CLAUDE.md's Missing-Verifier Gap Logging discipline. The gap entry's own
candidate design (a CNN predicting click-heatmap + directional-change-probs)
was built and shipped as SmallFrameChangeCNN, then rigorously A/B'd across 4
experiments today (REQ-ARC-FCP-5590/5728/5729/5730): a real dict-candidate
bug was fixed and found null, blend weight swept 40x and found null (localized
to a validation gate), the gate safely loosened and found still null (localized
to the scorer's own signal quality), and the scorer's held-out AUROC found to
be an action-id base-rate + seed-luck mirage matching REQ-ARC-WMTE-5727's
independent finding on hand-crafted linear features.

Status moves from open -> attempted_and_falsified: the specific frame-only CNN
design is closed (4 adversarially-verified negative results), but the
underlying need (action-efficient candidate ranking) is still open. Revised
candidate designs (patch-level interaction features, contrastive training
objective, multi-step history) are proposed but unbuilt -- any future attempt
must target a genuine representation change per Failed-Experiment Rerun
Discipline, not a retrain/re-tune of the falsified architecture.

